<h1 style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:800;">Domain Verification</h1>
<p>Verify your custom domain to start using it for branded short links.</p>

<h2>Step 1: Add Your Domain</h2>
<ol><li>Go to <strong>Settings → Domains</strong></li><li>Click <strong>Add Domain</strong></li><li>Enter your domain (e.g., <code>link.yourcompany.com</code>)</li></ol>

<h2>Step 2: Configure DNS</h2>
<p>Add the following DNS record at your domain registrar:</p>
<table><tr><th>Type</th><th>Host</th><th>Value</th><th>TTL</th></tr>
<tr><td>A</td><td>link</td><td><em>(shown in UTMPro)</em></td><td>3600</td></tr></table>
<p>Or use a CNAME record if preferred:</p>
<table><tr><th>Type</th><th>Host</th><th>Value</th><th>TTL</th></tr>
<tr><td>CNAME</td><td>link</td><td><code>go.utmpro.link</code></td><td>3600</td></tr></table>

<h2>Step 3: Wait for Verification</h2>
<p>UTMPro checks DNS records automatically every hour. Once verified, a green ✅ badge appears next to your domain. DNS propagation typically takes 15 minutes to 48 hours.</p>

<h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
<ul><li>Make sure there are no conflicting A or CNAME records</li><li>Check that your DNS provider supports the record type you're using</li><li>If using Cloudflare, turn <strong>off</strong> the orange proxy cloud (use DNS only)</li></ul>
